# mutgap3_sys_placement_unmap_bounds: An UnmapMemory (34) drops the task's placement-list mapping only when its range overlaps the list: offset < list end and list offset < end (in the service and in an in-process task). The placement list is at VA 6 * PAGE, 48 bytes (SetObjectAndPlacementList, 68), and an exec maps both lists. What the guest sees of the mapping: VA page 6's leaf is then made a hole, and an exec with no command buffers re-walks the page table only for a list whose mapping was dropped ("Failed to map placement list"), so it faults if it was dropped and completes if the old mapping is kept. First an unmap that starts exactly at the list's end (6 * PAGE + 48, one page long), then an unmap of the list's own page; the leaf is restored after each. Where the setups differ (the in-process tasks, and an unaligned unmap), that is locked too; each command waits for either outcome.
